      "test_mru_get_counts_as_use.py": {
        "kind": "intent_a",
        "rationale": "Change A adds MRUCache, which tracks use the same way LRUCache does: every read through __getitem__ marks the key as most recently used. On base+A, MRUCache inherits Cache.get, which reads through self[key], so get() counts as a use. Change B rewrites Cache.get to read the private data dict directly, bypassing __getitem__. B adds get() overrides only to the classes it knows about (LRUCache, LFUCache and the timed caches), not to the new MRUCache. In the merge, MRUCache.get() no longer records a use. Eviction and popitem then pick the wrong key."
      },
      "test_get_read_tracking_invariant.py": {
        "kind": "invariant",
        "rationale": "On every tree, get() on an LRUCache, and on a user subclass that records reads in __getitem__, must keep the read-tracking semantics that eviction relies on. This guards the shared get() path that both changes touch. It holds on base, A, B and the merge for LRUCache. The MRU-specific breakage is covered by the intent scenario."
      }
    }
  },
